# Dineros.cc — overview

Purpose
- Predictive budgeting and financial management with forecasting, registers, recurring items, reconciliation, reports, and integrations (Plaid, crypto).

Audience
- Maintainers and contributors working in Nuxt 4 + TypeScript
- AI agents and CI tooling (see AGENTS.md and .cursor/)

Tech stack
- App (app/): Nuxt 4 + Vue 3, TypeScript, Pinia, Tailwind CSS, @nuxt/ui, Vitest, Playwright
- Backend (Nitro/H3 in Nuxt server): TypeScript API routes under app/server/api
- ORM: Prisma 7 targeting MySQL 8; prisma-field-encryption for field-level encryption
- Data stores: MySQL 8, Redis 7/8
- Queues: BullMQ; scheduled jobs via nuxt-cron
- Integrations: Plaid, OpenAI, Postmark, optional NATS client
- Deployment: Docker (multi-stage), GKE (Kubernetes manifests in .deploy/), GitHub Actions (build, deploy, PR checks)

Packages and layout
- Monorepo via pnpm-workspace.yaml
  - app/ — main Nuxt application, APIs, Prisma schema/migrations, tests
  - microservice/ — companion service (migrate endpoints, limited schema, queues support)
  - scripts/, .deploy/, .github/ — automation, CI/CD, Kubernetes manifests

Key capabilities
- Forecast engine (app/server/services/forecast/*) with extensive tests
- Registers and entries with encryption and Plaid sync
- Recurrences with splits and transfer logic
- Reports and notifications
- Reconciliation flows
- Crypto wallet support and cash-on-hand tracking

Getting started
- Read README.md for local setup and commands
- For agents in constrained environments, read AGENTS.md (DB/Redis startup, env overrides)
